<article class="env-definition" id="02P1">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02P1">Definition <span data-tag="02P1">31.24.10</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a scheme. Let $\mathcal{L}$ be an invertible $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module. Let $s$ be a regular meromorphic section of $\mathcal{L}$. The sheaf of ideals $\mathcal{I}$ constructed in Lemma <a href="/tag/02P0" data-tag="02P0">31.24.9</a> is called the <em>ideal sheaf of denominators of $s$</em>. </p>
</article>